The `/playbook` skill's driving protocol carries the two untargeted chat-output rules as prose:
every id said in chat comes with its short title, filed items listed in the user's language, and an
experiment matrix runs in sized stages. The render is filtered to those two lines.

-- cmd --
sh -c 'booping render src/templates/skills/playbook.md.j2 | grep -E "^Every id you say in chat|^An experiment, eval or benchmark matrix"'
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
Every id you say in chat — an open item, an ADR, a rule, a plan — is followed by its short title; newly filed items are listed one per line, `Создан {id}: {title}` or `Created {id}: {title}` in the user's language ([booping:rule/0038](${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/specs/rule/0038-ids-carry-their-title.md)).
An experiment, eval or benchmark matrix runs in stages — cheap screen → shortlist → significance — and before each stage you name its size (calls, rough cost) and what it decides ([booping:rule/0039](${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/specs/rule/0039-experiments-run-in-stages.md)).
-- stderr --
